The sup over λ and over the conserved densities would need the explicit values of \(B(g,g)\) and \(C(g,g)\) for each \(\lambda\). Checking the endpoints is inconclusive: at \(\lambda\to 1/3\) the denominator of \(\beta_\lambda\) vanishes, so the supremum is likely attained at an interior point or in a limit, which I did not resolve.

